WEBVTT

00:00:07.830 --> 00:00:12.540
And please let me say one last thing.

00:00:14.040 --> 00:00:19.950
Mitsuo! I will kill you even If I have to
chase you down to the end of the earth!

00:00:28.160 --> 00:00:34.250
"Wave, Listen to Me!"

00:01:50.620 --> 00:01:53.200
Wow, wasn't that something?

00:01:53.200 --> 00:01:57.040
"Episode 2: I Despise Them"
I'd like to dedicate Yumi Matsutoya's
"Even If You Left Me" to her!

00:01:57.040 --> 00:02:00.750
Wow. That was great, miss.

00:02:00.750 --> 00:02:04.080
We're gonna have to settle this in court!

00:02:05.200 --> 00:02:06.540
Huh?

00:02:08.160 --> 00:02:09.040
What?

00:02:09.040 --> 00:02:10.540
"Dream Space of Bread and Curry"
"Floor Manager Minare Koda"

00:02:11.790 --> 00:02:13.290
"I, Minare Koda, will not complain no matter how
many people Mr. Mato shares the content of our
conversation with. Thank you for listening
to me vent. Thank you. I love you."

00:02:13.580 --> 00:02:15.870
Oh... Um...

00:02:16.870 --> 00:02:20.290
That place had great reviews
when I looked it up.

00:02:20.290 --> 00:02:22.250
I'll go try it out soon.

00:02:22.250 --> 00:02:26.000
And let's go drink again
when you finish your shift.

00:02:26.000 --> 00:02:28.290
Only if I'm not fired by then...

00:02:29.290 --> 00:02:32.450
"Mitsuo from Fukuoka"...

00:02:32.450 --> 00:02:35.040
What a coincidence.

00:02:37.120 --> 00:02:39.450
I'm getting hungry...

00:02:39.450 --> 00:02:40.250
"I, Minare Koda, will not complain
no matter how many people Mr. Mato
shares the content of our conversation with."

00:02:40.250 --> 00:02:43.750
"I, Minare Koda, will not complain
no matter how many people Mr. Mato
shares the content of our conversation with."
Would this count as a legally binding document?

00:02:43.750 --> 00:02:46.700
It can be used as proof in court, at least.

00:02:46.700 --> 00:02:49.500
As long as the fool gets fooled, I don't care.

00:02:49.500 --> 00:02:51.250
That's cruel.

00:02:51.250 --> 00:02:54.580
As a former TV industry guy,
your words are harsh.

00:02:54.580 --> 00:02:58.160
When she stormed in, was that
within your calculations, too?

00:02:58.160 --> 00:03:00.290
I wouldn't say calculations...

00:03:00.290 --> 00:03:02.160
I just had a feeling.

00:03:02.160 --> 00:03:05.620
I've actually been to that curry shop before.

00:03:05.620 --> 00:03:10.120
They had the radio on, playing our show.

00:03:10.120 --> 00:03:12.330
So, what did you think?

00:03:12.330 --> 00:03:14.620
The recorded portion was all right;

00:03:14.620 --> 00:03:17.830
I appreciated the fast-talking
drunk's top gear blabber.

00:03:20.450 --> 00:03:24.500
But things got dicey for me
the moment she stepped into studio 8.

00:03:24.500 --> 00:03:28.080
There was no script and
no time to come up with lines.

00:03:28.080 --> 00:03:31.040
Under those circumstances,
a total amateur pulled it off,

00:03:31.040 --> 00:03:32.950
leaving no room for me, the radio writer.

00:03:32.950 --> 00:03:35.330
Those are my thoughts.

00:03:35.330 --> 00:03:37.160
A rave review.

00:03:37.160 --> 00:03:40.700
Idiot. I'm telling you
never to bring her back again.

00:03:40.700 --> 00:03:44.330
Well, I'll be going to eat
at that place again soon.

00:03:44.330 --> 00:03:47.830
Then take Chishiro and Nanba with you, too.

00:03:47.830 --> 00:03:51.080
They seemed really into it.

00:03:52.750 --> 00:03:57.290
Minare Koda, huh? Let's hope
she's not fired and crying somewhere.

00:04:00.830 --> 00:04:02.950
I've got a few conditions for you.

00:04:02.950 --> 00:04:03.750
I'd do anything.

00:04:03.750 --> 00:04:06.040
Get off of that table,
wipe it down, and update the blog!

00:04:06.040 --> 00:04:10.250
Push the <i>tabatière </i>and ciabatta,
and stay quiet for the rest of the day!

00:04:11.160 --> 00:04:12.660
"Our crew at VOYAGER is trying hard not to melt
in the kitchen. Oh, look! Today's bread is ready!
Today, we're serving a French bread call '<i>tabatière</i>.'"

00:04:13.620 --> 00:04:14.620
Huh?

00:04:14.620 --> 00:04:15.620
"35 Comments"

00:04:16.660 --> 00:04:20.620
The voice I'm hearing on MRS right now
sounds just like you, Miss Koda.

00:04:20.620 --> 00:04:21.750
Is it just me who thinks that?

00:04:21.750 --> 00:04:24.330
I listened to September Blue Moon yesterday!

00:04:24.330 --> 00:04:26.160
Miss Koda, that was you,
wasn't it? It was great!

00:04:26.160 --> 00:04:28.700
On yesterday's broadcast, the woman
reminded me of the worker at Voyager...

00:04:28.700 --> 00:04:31.580
Please don't dis Fukuoka!

00:04:34.410 --> 00:04:35.750
Whoa! Wait a minute!

00:04:35.750 --> 00:04:38.580
Who remembers a restaurant
worker's voice and name?

00:04:38.580 --> 00:04:41.290
What kind of clientele do we have here?!

00:04:41.290 --> 00:04:45.410
Wait, maybe they see me
as a symbolic figure of this place.

00:04:45.410 --> 00:04:47.830
Manager, can I create an avatar of myself?

00:04:47.830 --> 00:04:50.450
Why can't you stay quiet for an hour?!

00:04:50.450 --> 00:04:52.040
In any case, don't forget...

00:04:52.040 --> 00:04:55.540
We own your life until
the summer festival ends, got it?!

00:04:55.540 --> 00:04:56.250
What?

00:04:56.250 --> 00:04:58.370
We got that food stall during
the summer festival.

00:04:58.370 --> 00:05:00.660
It'd be tough for Nakahara
to handle everything alone!

00:05:00.660 --> 00:05:01.370
So then...

00:05:01.370 --> 00:05:05.620
So make sure you secure another job until then!

00:05:05.620 --> 00:05:08.250
Out and out, he only thinks about himself!

00:05:08.250 --> 00:05:09.540
I mean, I'm the same, too.

00:05:09.540 --> 00:05:09.830
--Whatever happened to "compassion"?

00:05:09.830 --> 00:05:12.080
--It's not that surprising.
--Whatever happened to "compassion"?

00:05:12.080 --> 00:05:13.950
Think about it.

00:05:13.950 --> 00:05:18.500
The Odori Park Beer Festival happens
right after the Maruyama Summer Festival.

00:05:18.500 --> 00:05:19.620
Want some squid?

00:05:19.620 --> 00:05:20.750
No thanks.

00:05:20.750 --> 00:05:24.250
They say beer tastes like metal
when you're unemployed.

00:05:24.250 --> 00:05:27.370
At this point, I don't care
if beer tastes like rust.

00:05:27.370 --> 00:05:30.790
Let's come up with a way
so you don't get fired.

00:05:30.790 --> 00:05:33.620
Without you here, Miss Minare...

00:05:33.620 --> 00:05:35.910
...I wouldn't know what to do.

00:05:37.040 --> 00:05:38.620
You know, Nakahara...

00:05:38.620 --> 00:05:39.410
Huh?

00:05:39.410 --> 00:05:42.750
Do you know why we're doing a food stall
at the summer festival in Maruyama

00:05:42.750 --> 00:05:44.870
when we're based in Susukino?

00:05:44.870 --> 00:05:47.410
No, I never even thought to question it.

00:05:47.410 --> 00:05:50.450
This is something I heard
from Manager last year...

00:05:50.450 --> 00:05:53.160
Our curry soup...

00:05:53.160 --> 00:05:55.080
Ever since we opened, they've been
continuously adding broth to it.

00:05:55.080 --> 00:05:57.200
"Call the health center..."
Ever since we opened, they've been
continuously adding broth to it.

00:05:57.200 --> 00:06:00.160
"Call the health center..."
Seriously? And I'm the one
who makes the curry!

00:06:05.950 --> 00:06:09.200
Refined, as always.

00:06:09.200 --> 00:06:11.410
I'm not getting any younger.

00:06:11.410 --> 00:06:16.000
This is the last batch of soup
I can pass on to you.

00:06:16.000 --> 00:06:18.870
You weren't the best apprentice,

00:06:18.870 --> 00:06:21.910
but you worked harder than anyone else.

00:06:21.910 --> 00:06:24.830
The total opposite of my grandson who ran away.

00:06:24.830 --> 00:06:30.790
I can't be more relieved that your
restaurant will be succeeding Gagarin.

00:06:30.790 --> 00:06:32.790
Master...

00:06:32.790 --> 00:06:38.330
If the food stall that carries the Gagarin sign
at the Maruyama summer festival appears on TV,

00:06:38.330 --> 00:06:40.580
your grandson may see it.

00:06:40.580 --> 00:06:44.910
He won't be able to help but come back.

00:06:44.910 --> 00:06:46.660
Takarada.

00:06:46.660 --> 00:06:47.830
What are you...?

00:06:47.830 --> 00:06:53.410
Master, I am not that oblivious
when it comes to others' feelings.

00:06:53.410 --> 00:06:57.540
The one you truly desire as your successor...

00:06:57.540 --> 00:07:02.330
I just thought of that scenario
to entertain myself.

00:07:02.330 --> 00:07:06.700
Miss Minare, why don't you
re-evaluate the situation you're in?

00:07:06.700 --> 00:07:08.790
My situation...

00:07:08.790 --> 00:07:10.450
My situation?

00:07:10.450 --> 00:07:13.580
I don't know what to think of it...

00:07:14.870 --> 00:07:18.160
Excuse me, weren't you live on MRS yesterday?

00:07:18.160 --> 00:07:18.750
Uh... It must be somebody else.

00:07:18.750 --> 00:07:20.450
"What?"
Uh... It must be somebody else.

00:07:20.450 --> 00:07:24.160
But seriously. Is my voice
really that recognizable?

00:07:24.160 --> 00:07:30.200
It is. And that customer was totally here
when you stormed out that day.

00:07:30.200 --> 00:07:30.950
What...?

00:07:30.950 --> 00:07:32.830
"Staring..."

00:07:33.160 --> 00:07:34.950
Were you able to track down Mitsuo?

00:07:34.950 --> 00:07:36.830
Which one? Senda or Aida?

00:07:36.830 --> 00:07:37.830
"Results"

00:07:37.910 --> 00:07:42.450
Whoa! Why does everyone know it's me?
I only made one appearance on daytime radio!

00:07:42.450 --> 00:07:44.290
Is it going viral on SNS or something?

00:07:44.290 --> 00:07:46.870
It is strange. It's not like you mentioned
your name or anything.

00:07:46.870 --> 00:07:49.200
All this "love and attention"
is freaking me out!

00:07:49.200 --> 00:07:51.200
"Love is a weapon." Where was that from?

00:07:51.200 --> 00:07:53.410
Kazuo Umezu's "Iara."

00:07:53.410 --> 00:07:55.950
Look. Isn't this the guy
you exchanged cards with?

00:07:55.950 --> 00:07:56.540
Huh?

00:07:56.540 --> 00:07:57.540
"This comment is only visible to the administrator."
"This is Mato. Great job the other day.
Did you know about this video?"

00:07:59.410 --> 00:08:03.160
"A female worker storms out
when she hears herself on the radio."

00:08:03.290 --> 00:08:06.120
Old man!

00:08:06.120 --> 00:08:10.870
What the hell is that video? You took that, too,
didn't you? I bet you had an assistant with you.

00:08:10.870 --> 00:08:11.830
Rot in hell!

00:08:11.830 --> 00:08:14.120
I swear, it wasn't me.

00:08:14.120 --> 00:08:17.080
We're getting a lot of calls
regarding that, too.

00:08:17.080 --> 00:08:18.790
Are things booming over there, too?

00:08:18.790 --> 00:08:20.500
Glad to hear.

00:08:20.500 --> 00:08:23.870
Usage rights? I told you it wasn't me.

00:08:23.870 --> 00:08:27.410
I'll be going over there tonight
to talk it all over.

00:08:27.410 --> 00:08:29.410
That's right. To apologize.

00:08:29.410 --> 00:08:32.830
Mizu <i>manju </i>from Kashin? Ah, sure thing.

00:08:32.830 --> 00:08:34.160
You've got sophisticated taste.

00:08:34.160 --> 00:08:37.750
Hey, miss, are you even working tonight?

00:08:37.750 --> 00:08:42.290
What? Don't come until the summer
festival ends? Come on...

00:08:43.500 --> 00:08:46.790
That's more than a month away...

00:08:48.040 --> 00:08:50.580
Sounded like you were speaking
to your own daughter.

00:08:50.580 --> 00:08:53.500
My daughter's much more tame.

00:08:53.500 --> 00:08:55.370
Sure, sure.

00:08:56.750 --> 00:08:59.450
Are you trying to replace me?

00:08:59.450 --> 00:09:05.040
If that were to happen,
Kureko will strangle me to death.

00:09:05.040 --> 00:09:10.870
There's nothing to worry about. She's just a
total amateur who can speak without stumbling.

00:09:10.870 --> 00:09:12.950
But also...

00:09:14.950 --> 00:09:18.410
I just want to have that voice on deck.

00:09:18.410 --> 00:09:24.330
What listeners want to hear
on the radio is a voice like yours.

00:09:24.330 --> 00:09:29.870
There's a pleasant vibrato from the deepness of
your breath. It's the ideal reassuring whisper.

00:09:29.870 --> 00:09:32.580
Minare Koda's voice is the total opposite.

00:09:32.580 --> 00:09:35.410
It's at a higher register
that's alarming for the listeners.

00:09:35.410 --> 00:09:38.200
It's got an overbearing tone like an agitator.

00:09:38.200 --> 00:09:42.950
But despite all that, it wasn't unpleasant
for me. Which was strange.

00:09:42.950 --> 00:09:45.080
It put me in a space similar
to where I anticipate

00:09:45.080 --> 00:09:49.330
what my favorite female comedian's next line is.

00:09:49.330 --> 00:09:54.580
I'm just curious to test it out and see
if anyone else feels the same.

00:09:54.580 --> 00:09:57.910
I told you not to come
until the summer festival ended!

00:10:03.120 --> 00:10:06.660
According to the reviews, this place
was rated high for customer service.

00:10:06.660 --> 00:10:09.700
My apologies! I am planning on firing
her the middle of next month!

00:10:09.700 --> 00:10:11.620
Now I've got curry on the back of my head!

00:10:11.620 --> 00:10:13.750
Please take these vouchers for free side salads!

00:10:13.750 --> 00:10:15.580
Did he just jump over that?!

00:10:15.580 --> 00:10:17.910
Now, may I take your order?

00:10:17.910 --> 00:10:22.580
Sour chicken at spice level five with scones
and <i>tabatière</i>. And... a gin and tonic.

00:10:22.580 --> 00:10:28.000
A highball, croissant, sesame Kaiser roll,
King Birbar's <i>zangi, </i>and some edamame.

00:10:28.000 --> 00:10:32.540
Coconut-based seafood soup curry with <i>seelen</i>
and ciabatta. Oh, and a glass of red.

00:10:32.540 --> 00:10:35.410
Um... A mango lassi...

00:10:35.410 --> 00:10:38.580
Your orders are all over the place!
Are you trying to piss me off?

00:10:38.580 --> 00:10:39.950
But anyway...

00:10:39.950 --> 00:10:43.790
Mr. Mato, don't you feel some sense of
responsibility? The poor girl's getting fired.

00:10:43.790 --> 00:10:46.410
Sure, a little bit.

00:10:46.410 --> 00:10:48.950
Why don't you come with us?

00:10:48.950 --> 00:10:50.790
Huh?

00:10:50.790 --> 00:10:51.950
"Us"?

00:10:51.950 --> 00:10:56.950
Oh, right. I wasn't clear, was I?

00:10:56.950 --> 00:11:01.040
Why don't you come work with us in radio?

00:11:01.040 --> 00:11:02.580
Ah...

00:11:02.580 --> 00:11:03.370
What?!

00:11:03.370 --> 00:11:05.700
"Geegle Search"
"Radio Salary"
This <i>zangi </i>is spicy and delicious!

00:11:05.700 --> 00:11:06.910
"Geegle Search"
"Radio Salary"
It's up there, for sure.

00:11:06.910 --> 00:11:08.290
Radio...

00:11:08.290 --> 00:11:08.620
--Miss Minare, don't get
into that risky business!

00:11:08.620 --> 00:11:10.910
--How much is the pay...?
--Miss Minare, don't get
into that risky business!

00:11:10.910 --> 00:11:11.950
--Risky business...? That's harsh.

00:11:11.950 --> 00:11:13.910
--What's gonna happen to the
promise we made two years ago
--Risky business...? That's harsh.

00:11:13.910 --> 00:11:18.290
while we gazed at the snowy city from
the observation deck at Asahiyama Park?

00:11:18.290 --> 00:11:20.410
When Manager dies,
we'll franchise the restaurant,

00:11:20.410 --> 00:11:22.910
and color all of Hokkaido turmeric-yellow!

00:11:22.910 --> 00:11:25.750
You only started this March!

00:11:25.750 --> 00:11:28.290
"I was killed in that scenario..."
What makes you think I'm that
devoted to this curry restaurant?

00:11:28.290 --> 00:11:30.250
What makes you think I'm that
devoted to this curry restaurant?

00:11:30.250 --> 00:11:32.160
--And did you really say turmeric-yellow?
Couldn't you come up with something better?

00:11:32.160 --> 00:11:33.330
--Miss Koda.
--And did you really say turmeric-yellow?
Couldn't you come up with something better?

00:11:33.330 --> 00:11:34.250
Huh?

00:11:34.250 --> 00:11:38.790
Sounds like you secured your next job.
Congratulations!

00:11:38.790 --> 00:11:41.620
Now we have one less thing to worry about.

00:11:41.620 --> 00:11:43.450
Manager...

00:11:43.450 --> 00:11:45.120
No, Mr. Takarada...

00:11:45.120 --> 00:11:46.330
"Roaring..."
No, Mr. Takarada...

00:11:46.330 --> 00:11:50.500
"Height"
"Width"
"Thickness"
Whoa! That's an expression I've never seen before!

00:11:50.500 --> 00:11:53.790
Mr. Takarada...

00:11:53.790 --> 00:12:00.540
Thanks for bossing me around for the past
two years at barely minimum wage!

00:12:00.540 --> 00:12:02.200
From here on out--

00:12:02.200 --> 00:12:08.450
Well, at first, you'll be starting out
as my program's assistant once a week.

00:12:11.080 --> 00:12:17.200
From here on out,
you can cut my salary even more.

00:12:17.200 --> 00:12:20.620
I'll promote this place on the radio, too.

00:12:20.620 --> 00:12:21.620
What?

00:12:23.290 --> 00:12:24.700
Jeez...

00:12:27.000 --> 00:12:31.000
Am I going through menopause?
What's with my skin?

00:12:32.370 --> 00:12:40.200
"21 days until Minare Koda's
dismissal from Voyager."

00:12:41.660 --> 00:12:45.160
Oh... Good morning.

00:12:45.160 --> 00:12:46.330
Good morning.

00:12:46.330 --> 00:12:52.000
One whose heart is fulfilled doesn't
stay up late to browse horoscope sites.

00:12:52.000 --> 00:12:56.080
Let's see... "Your future lover
will appear riding a white elephant.

00:12:56.080 --> 00:12:58.330
By the way, elephant = car."

00:12:58.330 --> 00:13:00.830
What good is that metaphor?

00:13:00.830 --> 00:13:03.540
Ah well, let me save this.

00:13:03.540 --> 00:13:04.700
Good morning.

00:13:04.700 --> 00:13:05.910
Huh?

00:13:05.910 --> 00:13:08.200
Shall we get going then?

00:13:08.200 --> 00:13:09.160
"Elephant = car"...

00:13:09.160 --> 00:13:10.660
"The cool pose..."
"Elephant = car"...

00:13:10.660 --> 00:13:13.000
What?! So, it's you?!

00:13:13.000 --> 00:13:14.660
Oh, sorry.

00:13:14.660 --> 00:13:16.160
Mato was too busy.

00:13:16.160 --> 00:13:19.040
Oh, no, that's not what I meant.

00:13:19.040 --> 00:13:21.910
Um... Mr. Komoto... was it?

00:13:21.910 --> 00:13:22.540
The engineer?

00:13:22.540 --> 00:13:23.910
The mixer.

00:13:23.910 --> 00:13:26.750
He seems like the outdoors-type
on his days off.

00:13:26.750 --> 00:13:29.870
Not the friendliest, but he's pretty cute.

00:13:29.870 --> 00:13:32.330
Mr. Komoto, are you married?

00:13:32.330 --> 00:13:34.660
"A 165 km/h fast ball"
What? No, I'm single.

00:13:34.660 --> 00:13:37.620
You have a nice ride for being so young.

00:13:37.620 --> 00:13:40.410
He must have flexibility with his finances.

00:13:40.410 --> 00:13:42.950
This is the director's car.

00:13:42.950 --> 00:13:45.290
I commute with my bike over the summer.

00:13:45.290 --> 00:13:46.950
So you prefer horses over elephants.

00:13:46.950 --> 00:13:48.540
What are you talking about?

00:13:48.540 --> 00:13:51.450
I'm such an idiot. What am I thinking?!

00:13:51.450 --> 00:13:55.120
Now's definitely not the time
to start a new fling!

00:13:55.120 --> 00:13:57.250
Work, money, rent!

00:13:57.250 --> 00:14:00.660
On top of getting 500,000 out of my
800,000-yen savings stolen by my ex,

00:14:00.660 --> 00:14:04.250
I also face the crisis of unemployment!

00:14:04.250 --> 00:14:05.950
I need to get my priorities straight!

00:14:05.950 --> 00:14:10.250
If I keep this up, I'll be evicted
from my apartment by this fall!

00:14:10.250 --> 00:14:13.410
No! I just envisioned myself shoveling
snow at my parents' house!

00:14:13.410 --> 00:14:15.500
There's no way I'm going back to Kushiro!

00:14:15.500 --> 00:14:18.580
I want to stay in Sapporo where
the snow blower runs all night!

00:14:18.580 --> 00:14:22.120
--What?! What's wrong with her.
Why's she crying?
--I'll pay all the municipal tax!

00:14:22.120 --> 00:14:24.660
Hey, it's been 20 days since I last saw you.

00:14:24.660 --> 00:14:26.500
Well, I'll be at studio 4.

00:14:26.500 --> 00:14:28.700
All right. Thanks.

00:14:28.700 --> 00:14:30.950
So, you're finally here.

00:14:30.950 --> 00:14:33.910
You even sent a car over to get me.

00:14:33.910 --> 00:14:37.040
I totally forgot how it felt...

00:14:37.040 --> 00:14:41.160
It sure feels nice to be escorted by a man.

00:14:42.160 --> 00:14:44.370
The perks of being a woman, eh?

00:14:44.370 --> 00:14:45.370
Anyway, what do you think?

00:14:45.370 --> 00:14:47.080
Huh? Of what?

00:14:47.080 --> 00:14:50.330
Doesn't this room excite you?

00:14:52.450 --> 00:14:54.370
In terms of having a workplace affair?

00:14:54.370 --> 00:14:55.580
Of course not!

00:14:55.580 --> 00:14:59.830
Well, this is just radio.
It's not like it's TV or anything...

00:14:59.830 --> 00:15:03.370
Ah, listen to you.

00:15:03.370 --> 00:15:04.540
Minare...

00:15:05.500 --> 00:15:09.450
You've got nothing else to do.
Why don't you try talking in front of the mic?

00:15:13.370 --> 00:15:18.330
I'm here because you said you wanted to talk.
But now you're making me do all the talking?

00:15:20.870 --> 00:15:22.330
Huh?

00:15:22.330 --> 00:15:24.790
But why me?

00:15:24.790 --> 00:15:26.830
It feels nice to be invited,

00:15:26.830 --> 00:15:31.330
but it's rather reckless of you to drag
a curry restaurant worker into radio.

00:15:31.330 --> 00:15:35.080
There are plenty of other amateurs
out there who can talk.

00:15:35.080 --> 00:15:40.370
Am I just totally blanking that we hooked up
before that night at the bar?

00:15:40.370 --> 00:15:45.000
No. The very first time we met
was that night at the bar.

00:15:45.000 --> 00:15:47.950
Are you familiar with
the comedian Sissel Komei?

00:15:47.950 --> 00:15:53.580
Never heard of her. The name
sounds intimidating though.

00:15:53.580 --> 00:15:55.370
I see...

00:15:55.370 --> 00:15:58.580
Well, she was a comedian, back in the day.

00:15:58.580 --> 00:16:01.790
She was active over 30 years ago.

00:16:01.790 --> 00:16:06.330
She was the reason why
I switched to radio from TV.

00:16:06.330 --> 00:16:09.910
Ah, I see. So, my voice reminds you of hers?

00:16:09.910 --> 00:16:10.870
Nope, not at all.

00:16:10.870 --> 00:16:12.080
Then why bring it up?!

00:16:12.080 --> 00:16:13.410
Well, you know.

00:16:13.410 --> 00:16:17.330
I got bored with planning projects
for local idols and popular voice actors

00:16:17.330 --> 00:16:19.870
that didn't get a fair shake.

00:16:19.870 --> 00:16:22.790
I just felt like fostering
a voice talent from scratch.

00:16:22.790 --> 00:16:25.910
Wait, hold on. So, what about that comedian?

00:16:25.910 --> 00:16:26.700
Hey, seriously!

00:16:26.700 --> 00:16:32.620
These are the comments about you
that we received for Chishiro's program.

00:16:32.620 --> 00:16:37.620
We played two more recordings
of amateurs since your appearance,

00:16:37.620 --> 00:16:40.950
but yours got twice the reaction
than from both of the others combined.

00:16:40.950 --> 00:16:44.000
Reactions could've been good
because it was the first episode,

00:16:44.000 --> 00:16:48.830
but it's mostly because your talk
was the most entertaining and easy to hear.

00:16:48.830 --> 00:16:50.830
You may not recall,

00:16:50.830 --> 00:16:57.950
but in the 26 minutes and 10 seconds of
the bar recording and the live talk at studio 8,

00:16:57.950 --> 00:17:02.160
believe it or not, you never stumbled
over your words, not even once.

00:17:02.160 --> 00:17:06.790
That's nearly impossible for an amateur,
even with a script to rehearse with.

00:17:06.790 --> 00:17:11.580
As you can see from those comments, there were
voices that suspected it was all scripted.

00:17:13.620 --> 00:17:14.950
As for me...

00:17:14.950 --> 00:17:22.120
I just love that my recording of an amateur
did so well that people suspected it was a fake.

00:17:24.830 --> 00:17:27.870
You're asking me to talk,
but what do I talk about?

00:17:27.870 --> 00:17:32.500
Could I talk about my friend who thought "<i>mino</i>"
at a <i>yakiniku </i>restaurant was short for minotaur?

00:17:32.500 --> 00:17:35.910
Hmm, sounds fun, but maybe next time.

00:17:35.910 --> 00:17:41.750
I heard from the manager you guys are doing
a food stand at the Urasando Summer Festival.

00:17:41.750 --> 00:17:44.160
It's a good opportunity.
Why don't you promote that?

00:17:44.160 --> 00:17:45.540
What? Are you sure?

00:17:45.540 --> 00:17:49.620
The sponsor for that slot is the agency
that represents Chishiro.

00:17:49.620 --> 00:17:52.620
They wouldn't mind promoting a curry restaurant.

00:17:52.620 --> 00:17:55.910
But that's still not enough content,

00:17:55.910 --> 00:18:00.910
so why don't you talk about the highlights
of the festival, giving it your own spin?

00:18:00.910 --> 00:18:07.410
I'm not a huge fan of Urasando,
so it might come off a little harsh.

00:18:07.410 --> 00:18:09.370
Is that okay?

00:18:09.370 --> 00:18:12.160
Just be reasonable, got it?

00:18:15.540 --> 00:18:18.200
This isn't a live broadcast like last time.

00:18:18.200 --> 00:18:19.580
Be relaxed.

00:18:19.580 --> 00:18:22.160
It's for a small segment,
so five minutes will be enough.

00:18:22.160 --> 00:18:27.330
If there's something we can't use, I can
edit it out before sending it to mastering.

00:18:27.330 --> 00:18:32.700
Mr. Mato, it seems to me that you're certain
I'll eventually become a radio personality.

00:18:32.700 --> 00:18:34.830
Why do you think that?

00:18:36.120 --> 00:18:39.290
You used to address me as "miss."

00:18:39.290 --> 00:18:44.910
But today you've been calling me "Minare,"
like I'm your colleague or something.

00:18:44.910 --> 00:18:49.290
No, I always address
radio personalities with "miss."

00:18:49.290 --> 00:18:52.200
What?! Then treat me the same way!

00:18:52.200 --> 00:18:55.120
Minare, let's conquer...

00:18:55.120 --> 00:18:56.370
...the world.

00:18:56.370 --> 00:18:58.660
You're talking big for a local radio station.

00:18:58.660 --> 00:19:02.500
In reality, aren't you pressured
by live streaming services?

00:19:02.500 --> 00:19:04.700
That's enough. Let's get started.

00:19:04.700 --> 00:19:06.870
Three... two... one!

00:19:06.870 --> 00:19:08.040
Begin!

00:19:08.040 --> 00:19:10.870
Damn it everyone, how are you doing?!

00:19:12.750 --> 00:19:15.120
With only a week left in June,

00:19:15.120 --> 00:19:19.450
Hokkaido's long-anticipated
summer season is taking off!

00:19:19.450 --> 00:19:21.620
Speaking of summer, it's festival season!

00:19:21.620 --> 00:19:24.790
We've got three big festivals
in Sapporo coming up!

00:19:24.790 --> 00:19:27.660
The Hokkaido Shrine Festival,
Sapporo City Jazz, and, that's right!

00:19:27.660 --> 00:19:31.000
"Indian Dance"
The Urasando Summer Festival in Maruyama!

00:19:31.000 --> 00:19:32.750
"Indian Dance"
At Urasando, the high-end residential area

00:19:32.750 --> 00:19:36.700
where new luxury apartments are being built...

00:19:36.700 --> 00:19:38.410
A deplorable town, isn't it?

00:19:38.410 --> 00:19:40.660
--But regrettably, since it
is being held at such area,

00:19:40.660 --> 00:19:43.580
--So we're serving saffron rice, huh?
--But regrettably, since it
is being held at such area,

00:19:43.580 --> 00:19:46.040
--Since we can't bake the bread here.
--all the food is undeniably delicious!
That's the absolute truth.

00:19:46.040 --> 00:19:48.040
--Ide, could you help me with this?
--all the food is undeniably delicious!
That's the absolute truth.

00:19:48.040 --> 00:19:49.910
--Oh, yes!
--Of course, most of the food is from
restaurants located in Urasando.

00:19:49.910 --> 00:19:53.870
--Of course, most of the food is from
restaurants located in Urasando.

00:19:53.870 --> 00:19:57.000
When I went last year, I bought
a bottle of cheap red wine at Jupiter

00:19:57.000 --> 00:19:58.830
and attempted to eat at every stall!
First, I had paella...

00:19:58.830 --> 00:20:01.000
"Gagarin"
and attempted to eat at every stall!
First, I had paella...

00:20:01.000 --> 00:20:04.120
Miss Minare, isn't this "Gagarin"
the one you mentioned the other day?

00:20:04.120 --> 00:20:06.080
Yeah, that's right.

00:20:06.080 --> 00:20:08.540
Nakahara, could you adjust the curry soup?

00:20:08.540 --> 00:20:10.000
Ah, yes.

00:20:12.370 --> 00:20:15.040
Miss Minare, who made this soup?

00:20:15.040 --> 00:20:17.120
I don't remember making it...

00:20:17.120 --> 00:20:18.580
Huh?

00:20:18.580 --> 00:20:21.660
Miss Minare, um... Who's that over there?

00:20:21.660 --> 00:20:25.410
Ah, that must be the master's
grandson at Gagarin's.

00:20:25.410 --> 00:20:30.910
He couldn't help but come back when he saw
the young people putting up the Gagarin sign.

00:20:30.910 --> 00:20:33.120
So that was a true story?

00:20:33.120 --> 00:20:36.000
Have I ever lied to you before?

00:20:36.000 --> 00:20:38.750
I can recall 17 instances so far.

00:20:38.750 --> 00:20:40.620
What hour and minute, at what frame?

00:20:40.620 --> 00:20:42.870
This isn't what we should be arguing about!

00:20:42.870 --> 00:20:45.700
We open at noon, get back to curry headquarters.

00:20:45.700 --> 00:20:46.500
Will do.

00:20:46.500 --> 00:20:50.450
Urasando, I despise you but the food
is delicious! Build those luxury apartments!

00:20:50.450 --> 00:20:56.500
And that's how I conquered every food stall!
That's right! Take that!

00:20:58.370 --> 00:21:03.120
Ah, Miss Minare. Manager didn't
make this either, did he?

00:21:03.120 --> 00:21:05.830
Like I said, it's Mr. Takarada's master's curry.

00:21:05.830 --> 00:21:09.330
What? But Manager's curry
is a lot better than this.

00:21:09.330 --> 00:21:14.950
"Sizzle"
Gagarin continuously added broth
to their curry, and the successor of Gagarin

00:21:14.950 --> 00:21:17.290
is us, Voyager.

00:21:17.290 --> 00:21:18.580
That was the idea.

00:21:18.580 --> 00:21:22.450
But Mr. Takarada's abilities
surpassed the master's.

00:21:22.450 --> 00:21:28.500
"Sizzle"
So our freezer is packed with Gagarin's soup
because we don't use it anymore.

00:21:28.500 --> 00:21:30.290
But since it'd be a waste to throw it out,

00:21:30.290 --> 00:21:32.620
we use it during festivals like this
a few times a year.

00:21:32.620 --> 00:21:36.250
We make up some excuse
to use Gagarin's sign every time.

00:21:36.250 --> 00:21:40.450
So that dramatic scenario where the master's
grandson may come back was...

00:21:40.450 --> 00:21:42.000
Just some excuse.

00:21:42.000 --> 00:21:46.120
Jeez. That's horrible... Just plain cruel!

00:21:46.120 --> 00:21:50.410
More like... Who gives a crap, no?

00:21:50.410 --> 00:21:55.450
Ah! I almost forgot! Gagarin!
Make sure you try their soup curry!

00:23:43.950 --> 00:23:45.700
"Next Episode"
Hello, I'm Mizuho Nanba,
an assistant director at Moiwayama Radio.

00:23:45.700 --> 00:23:48.620
"Preview"
Hello, I'm Mizuho Nanba,
an assistant director at Moiwayama Radio.

00:23:48.620 --> 00:23:49.040
"Preview"
A virgin.

00:23:49.040 --> 00:23:52.040
"Preview"
Please stop. I just haven't
been in a relationship yet.

00:23:52.040 --> 00:23:57.410
Mizuho Nanba, she's the only sanctuary among
all the evil spirits lurking in this series.

00:23:57.410 --> 00:24:01.000
And what do you know,
she's being forced to live with me.

00:24:01.000 --> 00:24:05.410
Well, we're roommates now,
that's what it's called.

00:24:05.410 --> 00:24:07.790
Mizuho, I'll make love to you every night.

00:24:07.790 --> 00:24:09.870
What? Miss Minare?

00:24:09.870 --> 00:24:14.000
Next, on <i>Wave, Listen to Me!</i>:
"You All Are Soft."

00:24:14.000 --> 00:24:16.950
"See you next time!"
"Illustrated by Hiroaki Samura"
